    kind: work_item  # 3db1
    title: "agda: an anonymous module (module _ (X : Set) where) is emitted as a module named '_'; two in one file are split by occurrence, so deleting the first moves the second's stable_id"  # 3db1
    status: todo_hard  # 3db1
    priority: 4  # 3db1
    parent:  # 3db1
    tags:  # 3db1
    - analysis_quality  # 3db1
    - agda  # 3db1
    - stable_id  # 3db1
    isbefore: []  # 3db1
    duplicate_of: []  # 3db1
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 3db1
    pr_ref:  # 3db1
    description: "Found by the 2026-11-15 review of the stable-id items (reports and fixtures: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026). Re-run by hand the same day at dev e2b6ab8096, analyzer 9.2.0.\n\nDEFECT. REPRO, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/work/new/agda2/src/T.agda:\n\n    module T where\n\n    module _ (X : Set) where\n      f : Set\n      f = X\n\n    module _ (Y : Set) where\n      g : Set\n      g = Y\n\n`hypergumbo run` emits two `module` symbols named `_` (lines 3 and 7) with stable ids sha256:e603c60723cfdfde and\nsha256:83d2945312d70398, plus `f` and `g`. With the first anonymous module removed and the second left on line 7\n(work/new/agda3), the remaining `_` has stable id sha256:e603c60723cfdfde: its id moved to the value the deleted\none had.\n\nTWO THINGS WRONG. (1) An anonymous module is a scoping device, not a declaration with a name; `_` is not something\na reader can look up, and its members belong to the enclosing module. (2) Identity: the two tie on name and are\ntold apart by order, so an edit above changes the id of the one below. That is the property INV-fabih-nusus-sozad-zozor-sosiz-fazoh-mazoh-ponat's statement\ndescribes (\"deleting an earlier same-name sibling scope never moves another symbol's stable_id\"), here for Agda;\nINV-fabih-nusus-sozad-zozor-sosiz-fazoh-mazoh-ponat was fixed and closed for Scala, Kotlin, C# and Swift members.\n\nDECISION NEEDED before the fix: emit no symbol for an anonymous module (members attach to the enclosing module), or\nemit one whose identity comes from something that does not depend on order (its telescope text, for instance).\n\nACCEPTANCE. Deleting the first anonymous module of the fixture leaves every remaining stable id unchanged.\n\nNOT CHECKED: whether the members' own ids or scope chains include the `_` (on the fixture `f` and `g` are emitted\nwith bare names); how many anonymous modules agda-stdlib has."  # 3db1
    fields: {}  # 3db1
