  clock: 4  # 7e28
  nonce: '7e28'  # 7e28
  message: "Fixed in PR #2200. Re-ran the item's agda2 and agda3 fixtures: dev emitted two modules named `_` split by occurrence, and deleting the first moved the second's id (to e603c607...); now an anonymous module is not a symbol, its members belong to the enclosing module, and the remaining ids do not change on deletion. THE ITEM LEFT THE RULE OPEN; the choice (no symbol) was made in the package and is the owner's to overrule. Consequence: 1,085 `_` module symbols are gone on agda-stdlib and an anonymous module's parameters are in no scope chain. SEEN, not fixed (filed): a module's span is its header line, so `f` and `g` of the fixture are contained by the file node, not by `module T` (the same on dev). The change moves stable ids, so it shipped in the stableid v14 -> v15 bump; the spec's history row lists the rule and the measured share. Repro record (both arms, commands and copied outputs): ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/tracker/repros.md; per-package detail: pr2/STATUS.md; churn: pr2/final_measure.txt."  # 7e28
